          "lineage": "Hexabranchus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The Spanish dancer, scientific name Hexabranchus sanguineus (literally meaning \"blood-colored six-gills\"), is a dorid nudibranch, a very large and colorful sea slug, a marine gastropod mollusk in the family Hexabranchidae.The taxonomy of the genus Hexabranchus has been controversial but a thorough molecular and morphological study published in 2023 showed that the name H. Sanguineus was being used for at least 5 distinct species.",
